# Structuring Agricultural Education Research using Conceptual and Theoretical Frameworks.

**Authors:** Dyer, James E., Haase-Wittler, Penny S., Washburn, Shannon G.

## Abstract
Analysis of 348 articles from the Journal of Agricultural Education 1990-1999 showed that 83.3% used quantitative, applied survey research. Only 29% cited appropriate theoretical frameworks, 87% cited conceptual frameworks. They often cited limited references in establishing a framework and failed to relate findings to frameworks. (Contains 25 references.) (SK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ669194

